+/// Whether a clipboard shows `want` within ~0.6 s. Two that are one, such as a Wayland desktop's
+/// and its own Xwayland's (the compositor copies between them), take a moment to agree: read at
+/// once, they looked different, both were kept, and text written to one replaced what an app had
+/// just copied into the other (a file in Dolphin then pasted only as its address).
+fn shows_within(c: &dyn Clipboard, want: &str) -> MyResult<bool> {
+    for _ in 0..12 {
+        if c.get()? == want {
+            return Ok(true);
+        }
+        sleep(Duration::from_millis(50));
+    }
+    Ok(false)
+}
